@FEDept.BackendCourse.GroupA1.Api.Template_HostAddress = http://localhost:5117
@HttpsHostAddress = https://localhost:7135

GET {{FEDept.BackendCourse.GroupA1.Api.Template_HostAddress}}/health

###

### Confirm registration by magic link (copy the token from the link in Mailpit, http://localhost:8025)
POST {{HttpsHostAddress}}/auth/register/confirm
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "token": "replace-with-registration-token"
}

### Sign in (cookies are kept by the client between requests)
POST {{HttpsHostAddress}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "user@example.com",
  "password": "replace-with-password"
}

### Confirm sign-in with the OTP from Mailpit (http://localhost:8025)
POST {{HttpsHostAddress}}/auth/login/confirm
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "attemptId": "replace-with-attempt-id",
  "code": "replace-with-6-digit-code"
}

### Confirm sign-in with the token after #token= in the magic link
POST {{HttpsHostAddress}}/auth/login/confirm
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "token": "replace-with-attempt-id-and-secret"
}

### Send a new code or link (60 seconds after the last one)
POST {{HttpsHostAddress}}/auth/login/resend
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "attemptId": "replace-with-attempt-id"
}

### Refresh the token pair (uses the refresh_token cookie)
POST {{HttpsHostAddress}}/auth/refresh

### Sign out
POST {{HttpsHostAddress}}/auth/logout

###

# Cookies are `Secure`. Over plain HTTP, clients other than browsers on `localhost` may not send them back; use `--launch-profile https` and `https://localhost:7135` for refresh.
